Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• parties.case_id : key to join the parties table to the collisions table.  
• collisions.case_id : same key on collisions side.  
• parties.statewide_vehicle_type : tells us what kind of vehicle the party was operating / riding; filter with `LIKE '%motorcycle%'` to keep motor‑cycle parties only.  
• parties.party_type : make sure we keep only “driver” or “passenger” rows (i.e., the motor‑cyclists themselves).  
• parties.party_safety_equipment_1 / parties.party_safety_equipment_2 : contain the helmet information.  
  – Helmet used  → value contains the word “helmet” but not “not”.  
  – Helmet NOT used → value contains “helmet not used”.  
• collisions.motorcycle_collision (0 / 1) : another quick way to limit the analysis to crashes that involved at least one motorcycle.  
• collisions.motorcyclist_killed_count : number of motor‑cyclists killed in that crash – numerator for the fatality‑rate fraction.  
• collisions.case_id (in GROUP BY) : denominator is the number of distinct motorcycle collisions by helmet group.  

Typical conditions we will need  
1. Motorcycle collisions: ( collisions.motorcycle_collision = 1 ) or ( parties.statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%' ).  
2. Helmet used: ( parties.party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet%' OR parties.party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet%' )  
  AND NOT ( parties.party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%not%' OR parties.party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%not%' ).  
3. Helmet NOT used: ( parties.party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet not used%' OR parties.party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet not used%' ).  

Below are ten exploratory SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows) that gradually build up to the final computation.  
Each query is preceded by a short description.

```sql
--Description: 1) List the different vehicle types that appear in the parties table
SELECT DISTINCT statewide_vehicle_type
FROM parties
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 2) Inspect the distinct text values that appear in the first safety‑equipment column
SELECT DISTINCT party_safety_equipment_1
FROM parties
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 3) Inspect the second safety‑equipment column (may also mention helmets)
SELECT DISTINCT party_safety_equipment_2
FROM parties
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 4) Quick look at the motorcycle‑collision flag inside the collisions table
SELECT DISTINCT motorcycle_collision
FROM collisions
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 5) See how many crashes have at least one motorcyclist fatality
SELECT collision_severity,
       motorcyclist_killed_count
FROM collisions
WHERE motorcyclist_killed_count > 0
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 6) Fetch a sample of motorcycle parties together with helmet text
SELECT p.case_id,
       p.party_number,
       p.statewide_vehicle_type,
       p.party_safety_equipment_1,
       p.party_safety_equipment_2
FROM parties AS p
WHERE p.statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 7) Join parties and collisions to show helmet‑USED motorcycle crashes
SELECT DISTINCT c.case_id,
       c.motorcyclist_killed_count,
       p.party_safety_equipment_1
FROM collisions AS c
JOIN parties AS p
  ON c.case_id = p.case_id
WHERE c.motorcycle_collision = 1
  AND p.statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
  AND ( (p.party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet%' OR
         p.party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet%')
        AND
        NOT (p.party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%not%' OR
             p.party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%not%') )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 8) Join parties and collisions to show helmet‑NOT‑USED motorcycle crashes
SELECT DISTINCT c.case_id,
       c.motorcyclist_killed_count,
       p.party_safety_equipment_1
FROM collisions AS c
JOIN parties AS p
  ON c.case_id = p.case_id
WHERE c.motorcycle_collision = 1
  AND p.statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
  AND (p.party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet not used%' OR
       p.party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet not used%')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
--Description: 9) Aggregate: total motorcyclist fatalities & collisions when HELMET WAS USED
SELECT
       COUNT(DISTINCT c.case_id)                        AS motorcycle_collisions_helmet_used,
       SUM(c.motorcyclist_killed_count)                 AS motorcyclist_fatalities_helmet_used
FROM collisions  AS c
JOIN parties     AS p
  ON c.case_id = p.case_id
WHERE c.motorcycle_collision = 1
  AND p.statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
  AND ( (p.party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet%' OR
         p.party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet%')
        AND
        NOT (p.party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%not%' OR
             p.party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%not%') );
```

```sql
--Description: 10) Final query – compute the two fatality‑rate percentages side‑by‑side
WITH helmet_used AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT c.case_id, c.motorcyclist_killed_count
    FROM collisions AS c
    JOIN parties AS p ON c.case_id = p.case_id
    WHERE c.motorcycle_collision = 1
      AND p.statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
      AND ( (p.party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet%' OR
             p.party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet%')
            AND
            NOT (p.party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%not%' OR
                 p.party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%not%') )
),
helmet_not_used AS (
    SELECT DISTINCT c.case_id, c.motorcyclist_killed_count
    FROM collisions AS c
    JOIN parties AS p ON c.case_id = p.case_id
    WHERE c.motorcycle_collision = 1
      AND p.statewide_vehicle_type LIKE '%motorcycle%'
      AND (p.party_safety_equipment_1 LIKE '%helmet not used%' OR
           p.party_safety_equipment_2 LIKE '%helmet not used%')
)
SELECT
    (SELECT SUM(motorcyclist_killed_count) FROM helmet_used)*100.0 /
    (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM helmet_used)      AS pct_fatal_helmet_used,
    (SELECT SUM(motorcyclist_killed_count) FROM helmet_not_used)*100.0 /
    (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM helmet_not_used)  AS pct_fatal_helmet_not_used;
```
